{
  "uid": "hydra-runtime",
  "title": "Hydra \u2014 runtime, resources and scaling",
  "tags": [
    "hydra-lab",
    "runtime",
    "tuning"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 200,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Why RED is repeated on this board",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**This board exists for resource tuning and benchmarking (FR-078), which is why the RED row is duplicated at the bottom rather than left on its own board.**\n\nTuning a memory limit means reading heap, GC, container memory *and* latency at the same instant. Splitting them across two boards turns that into guesswork between screens \u2014 you end up correlating by memory of what the other tab looked like.\n\n**The container memory limit is not the maximum heap size.** Heap, class metadata, code cache, direct buffers, thread stacks and native allocations all live inside the limit. See `docs/memory.md` before concluding a pod needs more memory.\n\nBefore changing any request or limit, read `docs/resource-tuning.md` \u2014 in particular the rule that lowering a limit must be supported by measurement and must **not** be justified by the choice of concurrency model."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "JVM heap used vs committed",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service) (jvm_memory_used_bytes{jvm_memory_type=\"heap\"})",
          "legendFormat": "used {{service}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service) (jvm_memory_committed_bytes{jvm_memory_type=\"heap\"})",
          "legendFormat": "committed {{service}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service) (jvm_memory_limit_bytes{jvm_memory_type=\"heap\"})",
          "legendFormat": "max {{service}}",
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Agent runtime metrics. 'Committed' is what the JVM has taken from the OS; 'used' is what is live in it. A pod is OOMKilled on committed + non-heap, never on used."
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "JVM non-heap (metaspace, code cache, direct)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service, jvm_memory_pool_name) (jvm_memory_used_bytes{jvm_memory_type=\"non_heap\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}} {{jvm_memory_pool_name}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The memory people forget. Class metadata and the code cache grow with the application, not with the workload, and they are inside the container limit."
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "GC collections per second",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service, jvm_gc_name) (rate(jvm_gc_duration_seconds_count[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}} {{jvm_gc_name}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Collection frequency. Read with the panel to the right: frequent-and-short and rare-and-long are different problems."
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "GC pause duration",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, service, jvm_gc_name) (rate(jvm_gc_duration_seconds_bucket[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{service}} {{jvm_gc_name}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(jvm_gc_duration_seconds_sum[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "time in GC {{service}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "'Time in GC' is seconds of GC per second of wall clock \u2014 the number to compare against p99 latency on the row below. ZGC is in use; docs/jvm-flags.md explains why that choice is deliberately NOT made by this feature."
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Container memory vs limit",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (pod) (container_memory_working_set_bytes{namespace=\"hydra-app\", container!=\"\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{pod}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (pod) (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{namespace=\"hydra-app\", container!=\"\"})",
          "legendFormat": "limit {{pod}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "What the kernel sees, which is what the OOM killer acts on. Compare against the JVM heap panel: the gap is everything docs/memory.md accounts for."
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "title": "Container CPU vs request",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 20
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (pod) (rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{namespace=\"hydra-app\", container!=\"\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{pod}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "In cores. There is deliberately no CPU limit on these workloads: a CPU limit throttles rather than terminates, and CFS throttling on a JVM produces latency spikes indistinguishable from GC pauses \u2014 which would corrupt the benchmark. The HPA targets utilisation of the REQUEST."
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "title": "Replica count and HPA state",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "kube_deployment_status_replicas_available{namespace=\"hydra-app\"}",
          "legendFormat": "available {{deployment}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "kube_deployment_spec_replicas{namespace=\"hydra-app\"}",
          "legendFormat": "desired {{deployment}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "kube_horizontalpodautoscaler_status_desired_replicas{namespace=\"hydra-app\"}",
          "legendFormat": "hpa wants {{horizontalpodautoscaler}}",
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Driven by real observed metrics \u2014 nothing in this lab simulates a replica change (FR-070). If 'hpa wants' is flat while load rises, check the HPA's ScalingActive condition: no metrics is a different failure from no headroom (FR-072)."
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "title": "Pod restarts",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (pod) (kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{namespace=\"hydra-app\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{pod}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (pod) (kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{namespace=\"hydra-data\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{pod}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "A rising line here during a drill is the drill working. A rising line otherwise is a liveness probe killing a healthy-but-slow pod \u2014 which is why liveness depends on nothing external."
    },
